# Copy to /captures/config/fbui.env after actual TFT discovery and review.
# This is an intentionally invalid template and is never installed as active config.
# Replace fbN with the measured framebuffer identity (not guessed fb0/fb1).
REDUX_FRAMEBUFFER=/dev/fbN
REDUX_DASHBOARD_PORT=8080
REDUX_PIXEL_ORDER=rgb565
REDUX_ROTATE=0

# Extra flags appended to the fbui launch (word-split by systemd). Empty = the
# read-only status pages with swipe nav (taps need calibration).
#
# To enable TAPS + the interactive CONTROL DECK, run the one-command helper,
# which calibrates the panel (tap four corners + center) and turns the deck on:
#   sudo redux-deck-enable
# To do it by hand instead:
#   1. redux-display-diag --touch-device /dev/input/eventN --seconds 30 \
#        > /captures/config/diag.json   (tap TL, TR, BL, BR, center in order)
#   2. redux-touch-calibrate --report /captures/config/diag.json \
#        --output-dir /captures/config --confirm-order  → touch-calibration.json
# then set (and `systemctl restart redux-fbui`); --confirm-touch-calibration is
# REQUIRED alongside --calibration-file:
#   REDUX_FBUI_ARGS=--calibration-file /captures/config/touch-calibration.json --confirm-touch-calibration --deck
REDUX_FBUI_ARGS=
